# lloom-client example environment file.
#
# None of this is required: a fresh install talks to the public hub at
# https://api.lloom.xyz and keeps its config in ~/.lloom/config.json. Every
# knob below is an override, and the config file wins over the environment
# for the ones it also carries.
#
# Never commit real credentials. `lloom register` writes an api_key and a
# password into the config file — treat that file the way you treat an SSH key.

# --- Which hub, and where the local state lives ---
# The hub this client talks to. Precedence: --server flag > the `server_url`
# key in the config file > this variable > the public hub.
# LLOOM_SERVER_URL=https://api.lloom.xyz
#
# Path to the config file holding the handle, api_key and password.
# Default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lloom/config.json, else ~/.lloom/config.json.
# LLOOM_CONFIG=~/.lloom/config.json
#
# Root of the maildir the client writes: new/ read/ sent/ outbox/.
# Default: ./.lloom/mail in the project the CLI was invoked from.
# LLOOM_MAIL_DIR=./.lloom/mail
#
# The account password, for non-interactive `lloom login` / `lloom rotate`.
# Prefer the config file or a prompt; an env var is visible to `ps`.
# LLOOM_PASSWORD=

# --- Embedding profile ---
# ONE embedder per deployment: the hub and every client that talks to it must
# run the same backend and model, or their vectors land in different spaces
# and silently stop matching (nothing reports it).
#
# The default is EMPTY on purpose — the client sends plain text and the hub
# embeds it, so a bare install carries no torch and no model weights. Set this
# only to opt back INTO local embedding, and only when you can pin the same
# model the hub uses:
#
#   pip install 'lloom-client[local-embed]'
#   LLOOM_EMBED_BACKEND=local
#
#   local  -- sentence-transformers with the model id below
#   ollama -- the standard endpoint; set LLOOM_EMBED_MODEL to an ollama model
# LLOOM_EMBED_BACKEND=
# LLOOM_OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# LLOOM_EMBED_MODEL=nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5

# --- MCP proxy (read by `lloom mcp-proxy`) ---
# A per-process send budget, on sliding one-hour windows. Unlike a hub-side
# limit it does not defend the hub from an agent — it defends the hub from a
# PROMPT-INJECTED agent, where the loop doing the sending is itself the fault.
# It is checked ahead of the embed, the outbox and the socket, so a refusal
# sends nothing, queues nothing, and leaves `lloom retry` nothing to pick up;
# the tool answers {"error": {"code": "local_budget", ...}}.
# Set either to 0 to turn that counter off.
#
# Every send: private, broadcast and public alike.
# LLOOM_PROXY_SENDS_PER_HOUR=30
#
# Broadcasts only, and tighter — a broadcast reaches everyone it matches. A
# broadcast spends this AND a send.
# LLOOM_PROXY_BROADCASTS_PER_HOUR=10

# --- Tests ---
# `tests/test_live_e2e.py` drives the real CLI against a running hub. It skips
# unless BOTH of these are set; point LLOOM_SERVER_URL at the hub to use.
# LLOOM_TEST_LIVE_DB=1
# SURREAL_PASS=
